WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
Two cells carry the same genome.

2
00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.620
Why can they read different genes?

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.740
Watch one gene in each nucleus.

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.580
The DNA sequence matches.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.900
Yet one cell makes many messenger RNA molecules, while the other makes almost none.

6
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.760
The puzzle is not missing genes.

7
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.180
It is selective use.

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.900
Eukaryotic DNA is packed into chromatin.

9
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.880
Blue DNA wraps around gold nucleosomes.

10
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.980
Packing does not make every gene permanently silent.

11
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.680
It makes access conditional.

12
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.640
Proteins must reach the promoter before transcription can begin.

13
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.020
Packed DNA is harder, not impossible, to read.

14
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.170
Remodelling complexes can move nucleosomes.

15
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.530
As one gold block slides aside, the white promoter becomes reachable.

16
00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:06.490
Some pioneer factors can bind nucleosomal DNA, so access and regulator binding can

17
00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:07.550
influence each other.

18
00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.250
The promoter stays fixed while nucleosomes shift around it.

19
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.360
Access is only one requirement.

20
00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.340
A teal enhancer can sit far from the promoter.

21
00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:25.780
Sequence-specific transcription factors bind the enhancer and recruit coactivators.

22
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:32.380
Mediator helps connect these regulators with RNA polymerase II at the promoter.

23
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.440
The enhancer itself is DNA, not a diffusible protein.

24
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:45.383
Now predict. Matching enhancer factors are present, but a nucleosome still covers

25
00:01:45.383 --> 00:01:49.023
the promoter. Is strong transcription guaranteed?

26
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:54.423
Hold both requirements in view: regulatory assembly and access.

27
00:01:55.803 --> 00:01:57.503
Decide before the machinery moves.

28
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.640
No, not in this simplified case.

29
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:12.060
The matching factors supply regulatory information, but the covered promoter remains

30
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.480
hard to use. Bound factors can recruit a remodeller.

31
00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.940
Once it shifts the nucleosome, the assembled regulators can help raise

32
00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:22.940
transcription.

33
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.360
Enhancers often act by combinations.

34
00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:31.440
Picture a committee whose decision depends on which members arrive.

35
00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.460
One factor alone may do little.

36
00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.280
Two together may recruit machinery effectively.

37
00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.900
Different cells supply different combinations.

38
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:44.623
Return to the two cells.

39
00:02:45.923 --> 00:02:47.123
Their DNA still matches.

40
00:02:48.503 --> 00:02:52.503
In the liver cell, the needed factors and accessible promoter coincide.

41
00:02:53.983 --> 00:02:56.703
In the kidney cell, a needed factor may be missing.

42
00:02:57.983 --> 00:03:00.263
A repressor could also explain low output.

43
00:03:01.317 --> 00:03:05.097
A reporter assay can test these pieces beside a promoter.

44
00:03:06.397 --> 00:03:10.757
Deleting a piece tests necessity, and testing it alone tests sufficiency.

45
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:16.717
Combining pieces tests cooperation, and reversing one tests orientation.

46
00:03:17.957 --> 00:03:20.837
But the assay moves DNA from its native setting.

47
00:03:22.097 --> 00:03:24.917
A genomic deletion is a stronger test there.

48
00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.360
The same genome can therefore support different outputs.

49
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.340
Chromatin changes reachability.

50
00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.960
Enhancer-bound regulators change recruitment, including recruitment of enzymes that

51
00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.000
change reachability.

52
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.740
Neither layer works as a universal switch.

53
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.740
Together they make gene use conditional on cell state.
